      "side": 0,
      "message": "Yes and no.\n\nFor the mainline module, we are using MdnsMultinetworkSocketClient, and the passed-in SocketKey is the same as the CacheKey it has. The MdnsDiscoveryManager#handleOnResponseReceived has a check to ensure that.\n\nHowever, GMScore is using MdnsSocketClient, which means that MdnsDiscoveryManager#getMdnsServiceTypeClient returns all service type clients and passes a SocketKey to process a response. The passed-in SocketKey might be different from the CacheKey. Therefore, this is a behavior change for GMScore. I think the problem is that this change returns incorrect service type clients that are unrelated to the SocketKey in `getMdnsServiceTypeClient()`.\n\nhttps://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Connectivity/+/2593907/6/service-t/src/com/android/server/connectivity/mdns/MdnsDiscoveryManager.java\n\nUnfortunately, we didn\u0027t have a way to verify the design with MdnsSocketClient before. Thanks for figuring out a way to run the test with MdnsSocketClient.",
